From 8532e40be5a3c4d1063255a69e042264b26ee685 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Baker <ConnorBaker01@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:29:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: complete public dependency discovery for split
 installations

Build on NVIDIA/cudnn-frontend#482, whose imported CUDA dependency removes
producer include paths from exports. Use the bundled CUDNN::cudnn target
instead of CuDNN::CuDNN, install its finder, and share producer/consumer
discovery. Resolve separately installed NVRTC headers and optional JSON.

Respect optional and quiet package lookups, including retries after partial
discovery, without losing required checks while building the producer.

Upstream-PR: https://github.com/NVIDIA/cudnn-frontend/pull/482
---
 CMakeLists.txt                             | 21 +++---
 cmake/cuDNN.cmake                          | 80 ++++++++++------------
 cmake/cudnn_frontend-dependencies.cmake.in | 35 ++++++++++
 cudnn_frontend-config.cmake.in             |  7 +-
 4 files changed, 86 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 cmake/cudnn_frontend-dependencies.cmake.in

